    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: 02c79889d3894e72ca442bfe41c188d588a18544 -->\n**Needs changes before merge** (one process item: no `PROCESS_VERSION` bump).\n\n**Blockers**\n1. `xtask/src/tests.rs` is under `xtask/`, a process file (AGENTS.md \"Process changes bump `PROCESS_VERSION`\"). `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION` is still `16` on this branch and main. Bump it to the next free number (`17` if nothing else has taken it at merge time) and the PR needs no other change. This is the same item the earlier contributor-agent review raised, and it is still open.\n\n**What looks good**\n- `crates/app/tests/operations.rs` header now names `motion::drilling, finishing3d, machining2d, machining3d, multiaxis, plunge_law`. The `//!` change is comment-only.\n- The new xtask test `a_motion_generator_change_selects_the_operations_suite` passes, and it fails when the header is reverted to main's: `operations.rs must name motion::machining2d` (I checked this in the worktree, then restored the PR's file).\n- A probe with a `crates/motion/src/multiaxis/mod.rs` change selects app suites including `operations`; no suite is dropped compared with the plan before the header change.\n\n**Local results** (trial merge with current origin/main, clean merge, GitHub reports MERGEABLE)\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `cargo test -p xtask` | 34 passed, 0 failed |\n| `cargo clippy -p xtask --all-targets -- -D warnings` | clean |\n| `operations` suite | not run: the change to it is a `//!` comment line only |\n\n**Notes (not blocking)**\n- The PR body says 34 tests; that matches this run.\n- The probe used the merged tree, so `cargo xtask gate quick` fell back to batch (`Cargo.toml` came in with main); the selection check was made by the new test on `quick::plan` directly, which does not depend on that.\n\nA maintainer will approve and merge by hand.\n",
